## Sync

One relay, remembered, and explicit verbs. Nothing runs in the background.

  dark sync setup                  # name this instance, point it at a relay, push once
  dark sync                        # push then pull
  dark push / dark pull            # one direction only
  dark commits                     # THIS branch's commits, newest first
  dark review pull [queue]         # stage a peer's ops instead of applying them

Ops are content-addressed, so pushing the same work twice changes nothing.
Pulled code is ordinary package code: it does not run until you run it, and
the unguarded HTTP transport it could reach is limited to the relay you
configured, not whatever it asks for.
  (see: docs scm)



Running things follow your edits WHEN ASKED. `apps view <Module> --live` opens any module with
`init`/`update`/`render` as a live view; save an edit to it or its callees and it
repaints. `serve <router>` runs the newest router that passes its checks on every
request with `--live`; a broken save keeps the previous one serving. The
workbench shows `// = value` beside calls from the last recorded run.